FAIL is grounded in #4 only: 3 of the 9 named fix sites (chart-walk
hcAmt/livingMonth/spend in buildBudgetVsActualChartData) lack any
regression test, violate the task's own written mutation-or-provably-
unobservable acceptance bar, and I demonstrated a live -0 leak into the
budget-vs-actual chart's JSON at those exact 3 sites pre-fix using the
real classifier pipeline. Remedy: add an HTTP- or function-level test
(budget settings configured so the rawCombinedTarget>0 gate is cleared,
or a direct buildBudgetVsActualChartData call) asserting no "-0" token in
the chart JSON for a cancelling healthcare/living month, mirroring the
existing cb9_negzero_http_test.go pattern.

Observations for backlog (NOT FAIL grounds — different files/packages,
predate CB9, outside CB9's written scope):
- internal/services/insights/trends.go direct SumAmount() negations feed
  mcpsvc/spend/trends.go's round2(), which does not normalize -0; a
  period whose outflows cancel exactly emits literal `-0` in the MCP
  get_trends velocity JSON (dailyAvg/historicalDaily). round2 has no -0
  belt anywhere in mcpsvc/spend/insights.go.
- internal/templates/render.go formatNumber has the same %.0f-honors-
  sign-bit bug as formatMoney/formatPercent had pre-CB7/CB9, currently
